WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:05.040
Halloween is fast approaching, and it's bringing
a ton of new horror movies to terrify you.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.500
Here's how the theaters will trick and treat
you this Halloween.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:10.000
The Nun

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:16.340
The Conjuring Universe is screaming back into
theaters with The Nun, which will add some

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:18.700
backstory to one of Conjuring 2's most terrifying
characters.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:24.260
A priest joins forces with a young nun in
Romania to investigate a death at a remote,

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:26.560
probably haunted abbey in the mountains.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:32.060
You can bet they'll come face to face with
a few unholy horrors creeping around those

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:32.640
dark hallways.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.200
And they are having nun of it.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:41.500
American Horror Story's Taissa Farmiga plays
the lead, with Bonnie Aarons returning as

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:42.180
the demonic nun Valak.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.780
The Nun will return to scare the pew out of
you on September 7th.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:48.280
Mandy

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:53.820
When critics rave that Nicolas Cage gave "the
performance of a lifetime," you know it's

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.620
something special.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:55.600
"So what you hunting?

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.360
"It's Crazy evil!"

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:04.680
From writer-director Panos Cosmatos, Mandy
is a tale of backwoods revenge that pushes

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:08.520
the horror envelope in ways few filmmakers
would even attempt.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:12.700
Red and Mandy lead an isolated existence deep
in the woods.

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:18.040
That is, until Mandy breaks that cardinal
rule of camping she attracts the attention

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:19.520
of a psychotic cult leader.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:24.880
Obviously, things go bad, leading Red to embark
on a spree of drug-fueled vengeance.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:30.340
Behold the insanity when Mandy debuts September
14th.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:31.780
Halloween

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:37.380
Remakes and reboots of classic horror franchises
haven't exactly been cinematic gold in recent

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:42.560
years, but Halloween might be the horror movie
that finally, violently breaks the mold.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:47.660
Eastbound &amp; Down star Danny McBride and producer
David Gordon Green came together to work on

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:52.460
the concept for the new film, which they pitched
directly to the franchise's original creator

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:57.500
John Carpenter, who loved it, even though
he never wanted a sequel in the first place.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:58.460
Why this time?

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.780
"It's pretending the other sequels didn't
happen."

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:07.040
This new film takes place after the events
of the 1978 original, and judging by the trailers,

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:09.240
Halloween is going to be pure terror.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:12.000
Take a look when it hits theaters on October
19th.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:13.360
Overlord

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:19.420
A World War II-set horror outing from J.J.
Abrams' Bad Robot production company, Overlord

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:24.620
asks the question: what's worse than dropping
into a German-filled warzone?

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:30.460
Simple: dropping into a German-filled warzone
along with goopy zombie-monsters.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:35.700
The movie follows some American paratroopers
who land in German-occupied France and find

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:38.640
themselves fighting for their lives against
bloodthirsty monsters.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:43.900
Since this is a Bad Robot production, it wasn't
long before rumors started flying that Overlord

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:46.980
was yet another stealth entry in the Cloverfield
universe.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:50.880
Despite the speculation, J.J. Abrams says
it definitely isn't.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:56.220
And that's totally okay: a World War II survival
horror movie sounds like a great time all

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:56.980
by itself.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.840
Check it out when Overlord premieres on November
9th.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:01.320
The Predator

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:07.200
The original Predator immersed audiences in
an exciting blend of sci-fi, action, and horror,

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.500
and the sequel looks like it's going back
to those terrifying roots.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:15.760
Co-writer and director Shane Black promises
that The Predator will carry a hard R rating,

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:20.360
giving the alien hunter free reign to do what
it does best: take loads of guys.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:29.160
The film's suburban setting should provide
even more opportunities for thrills, because

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:33.460
the scariest monster is the one in your own
backyard… and we don't mean your Weird Uncle

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.040
Charlie.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:38.800
Activate your heat vision and look for The
Predator in theaters on September 14th.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:39.860
Venom

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:45.260
While it may not be a horror movie in the
classic sense, Venom is shaping up into something

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:45.760
terrifying.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:51.620
Director Ruben Fleischer is promising a horror-tinged
film with a Venom who isn't afraid to get

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:53.360
bloody and chomp on a few heads.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:56.140
"So many snacks, so little time."

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:03.760
All signs point to Sony getting things right
with their second crack at the deadly symbiote

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:07.820
and we'll see just how right when Venom
hits theaters on October 5th.

